18350"><a title="Search site" class="mega-menu-link" href="https://obr.uk/site-search/"><i class="far fa-search"></i></a></li></ul></div></div></div><div class="cell small-6 medium-3 large-4 columns text-right"><ul id="quick-links" class="dropdown menu float-right" data-dropdown-menu data-alignment="right"><li class="is-dropdown-submenu-parent"> <a href="#">Recent publications</a><ul class="menu"><li><a href="https://obr.uk/download/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-march-2026/?tmstv=1793370306" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-pdf"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp; Latest EFO</a></li><li><a href="https://obr.uk/download/fiscal-risks-and-sustainability-report-july-2026/?tmstv=1793370306" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-pdf"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp; Latest FRS</a></li><li><a href="https://obr.uk/download/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-october-2026/?tmstv=1793370306" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-pdf"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp; Economic and fiscal outlook – October 2026<li><a href="https://obr.uk/download/welfare-trends-report-june-2026/?tmstv=1793370306" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-pdf"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp; Latest WTR</a></li></ul></li></ul></div></div></div></nav></div></div><main id="pagecontent" class="container" role="main"><div id="main"</div><section id="main-hero" class="hero hero-home hero-super hero-efo bg-efo-light"><div class="grid-container"><div class="grid-x grid-padding-x row-hero align-top hero-content"><div class="small-12 medium-8 cell"><p class="date"> | <time>28 October 2026</time></p><h1 class="news-heading"><a href="	https://obr.uk/efo/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-october-2026/">Rising energy prices and interest rates drive higher government borrowing</a></h1><p>Energy prices have risen sharply this year, pushing up inflation, lowering real incomes, and reducing GDP growth next year. Higher inflation and interest rates drive up the forecast for government borrowing. Budget decisions further increase borrowing in the near term and reduce it in the medium term. As a result, borrowing is forecast to fall to around 2% of GDP in the medium term, but at a slower near-term pace than previous plans. This would stabilise debt though at an elevated level. The fiscal mandate is met with a reduced margin which is small relative to risks around the forecast.</p></div><div class="small-12 medium-4 cell"><div class="available-downloads"><h2>Available downloads</h2><ul class="no-bullet"><li><p><a class="download-link" title="Economic and fiscal outlook – October 2026" href="https://obr.uk/download/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-october-2026/?tmstv=1793370306" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-pdf"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;Economic and fiscal outlook – October 2026</a></p></li><li><p><a class="download-link" title="October 2026 Economic and fiscal outlook – charts and tables: zip file" href="https://obr.uk/download/october-2026-economic-and-fiscal-outlook-charts-and-tables-zip-file/?tmstv=1793370306" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-archive"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;October 2026 Economic and fiscal outlook – charts and tables: zip file</a></p></li><li><p><a class="download-link" title="October 2026 Economic and fiscal outlook – detailed forecast tables: zip file" href="https://obr.uk/download/october-2026-economic-and-fiscal-outlook-detailed-forecast-tables-zip-file/?tmstv=1793370306" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><i class="far fa-file-archive"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;October 2026 Economic and fiscal outlook – detailed forecast tables: zip file</a></p></li></ul> <a href="" class="ad-cta">See all available downloads</a></div></div></div></div></section><section id="main-hero-cta" class="hero-cta hero-home-cta hero-super-cta hero-cta-efo bg-efo-dark"><div class="grid-container"><div class="grid-x row-hero align-middle"><div class="small-12 cell"><h3 class="hero-cta-title left"></h3><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Economic and fiscal outlook press briefing: watch again below or download the <a href="https://obr.uk/docs/sodugn2q